  "challenge": "HTML-002",
  "task": "Create a semantic table of two mountains.\n\nUse one table with caption `Mountain heights`, a thead row of two th elements `Mountain` and `Height (m)` with scope=\"col\", and a tbody with two rows in this order: `Fuji`, `3776`; `Kilimanjaro`, `5895`. Each body row starts with a th with scope=\"row\", followed by a td for the height. No additional rows or cells.\n\nUse only HTML in this file; no JavaScript or CSS is needed. Keep the specified text, element order and attributes. Checks inspect the parsed DOM; whitespace and attribute order do not matter.\n\n## Example\n\nThe table has two columns headed `Mountain` and `Height (m)`. Its first body row reads `Fuji | 3776`, followed by `Kilimanjaro | 5895`. The caption reads `Mountain heights`.\n",
  "language": "html",
  "file": "page.html",
  "starter": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Mountain</td>\n    <td>Height (m)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Fuji</td>\n    <td>3776</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Kilimanjaro</td>\n    <td>5895</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n",
